  "nabr:part3.ch2#b0": {
   "id": "nabr:part3.ch2#b0",
   "kind": "nabr.block",
   "section": "nabr.part3.ch2",
   "path": [],
   "fields": [],
   "raw": {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "ar": "نبر الحرف هو الذي يقع على **اللفظ القرآني** من حيث نطقه نطقًا سليمًا يليق بقدسيته، بلا عوج ولا إخلال ولا تمييع.",
    "en": "Letter stress acts on **the Qurʾānic word itself**, ensuring it is pronounced soundly and fittingly, with no distortion, defect or slurring."
   },
   "hash": "84fca4aa6649a735"
  },
  "nabr:part3.ch2#b1": {
   "id": "nabr:part3.ch2#b1",
   "kind": "nabr.block",
   "section": "nabr.part3.ch2",
   "path": [],
   "fields": [],
   "raw": {
    "type": "section",
    "titleAr": "أولًا: نبر ترتيب الحروف — (أ) نبر منع الاختلاس",
    "titleEn": "I. Ordering the letters — (a) preventing clipping"
   },
   "hash": "e84ea8d0af4af66c"
  },
  "nabr:part3.ch2#b2": {
   "id": "nabr:part3.ch2#b2",
   "kind": "nabr.block",
   "section": "nabr.part3.ch2",
   "path": [],
   "fields": [],
   "raw": {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "ar": "هو الذي يحمي الكلمة من الاختلاس الصوتي ويرتّب حروفها ترتيبًا تستسيغه الأذن، وقواعده هي القواعد العامة السابقة. ويدلّ على ذوق القارئ ومهارته، والأصل فيه التلقّي المتصل إلى رسول الله ﷺ.",
    "en": "This protects the word from phonetic clipping and orders its letters so the ear finds them natural. Its rules are the general rules already covered. It reveals the reciter's taste and skill, and its foundation is the unbroken oral chain back to the Prophet ﷺ."
   },
   "hash": "7c3e9f9248e9aa9f"
  },
